            "id": "4946619",
            "title": "Wall Street Lunch: AI Regulation Hopes Fade After Trump Calls AI Concerns A 'Hoax'",
            "description": "<html><body><p data-eci=\"true\"><figure class=\"getty-figure\" data-type=\"getty-image\"><picture> <img alt=\"Artificial Intellegence\" data-id=\"2032367897\" data-type=\"getty-image\" fetchpriority=\"high\" height=\"1024\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 132px), (max-width: 1199px) calc(100vw - 666px), (max-width: 1307px) calc(100vw - 708px), 600px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2032367897/image_2032367897.jpg?io=getty-c-w630\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2032367897/image_2032367897.jpg?io=getty-c-w1536 1536w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2032367897/image_2032367897.jpg?io=getty-c-w1280 1280w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2032367897/image_2032367897.jpg?io=getty-c-w1080 1080w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2032367897/image_2032367897.jpg?io=getty-c-w750 750w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2032367897/image_2032367897.jpg?io=getty-c-w640 640w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2032367897/image_2032367897.jpg?io=getty-c-w480 480w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2032367897/image_2032367897.jpg?io=getty-c-w320 320w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/2032367897/image_2032367897.jpg?io=getty-c-w240 240w\" width=\"1536\"/> </picture><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"> </p> <p class=\"item-credits\">D-Keine/iStock via Getty Images</p></figcaption></figure></p> <p>Listen below or on the go on <a href=\"https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/wall-street-breakfast/id1358381502\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">Apple Podcasts</a> and <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/show/05uLjJxkVgQsRk8LWLCLpx?si=r3_yJgxiQiivJwNQG8WNew&amp;nd=1\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">Spotify</a></p> <p></p><div class=\"pcast hidden-print\">\n<div class=\"pcast__section-1\">\n<img alt=\"\" class=\"pcast__top-img pcast__marketing\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2018/11/21/podcast_series_header.png?io=w640\"/>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pcast__section-2\"><iframe frameborder=\"0\" height=\"200px\" sap-id=\"4\" src=\"https://widget.spreaker.com/player?episode_id=75149498&amp;theme=light&amp;playlist=false&amp;playlist-continuous=false&amp;chapters-image=true&amp;episode_image_position=right&amp;hide-logo=true&amp;hide-likes=true&amp;hide-comments=true&amp;hide-sharing=true&amp;hide-download=true&amp;color=ff6900\" title=\"Trump says AI takeover is a hoax\" width=\"100%\"></iframe></div>\n<div class=\"pcast__section-3\">\n<div class=\"pcast__ad-container\"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>A Trump <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4642717-trump-calls-ai-a-hoax-in-surprise-onstage-call-with-nvidias-jensen-huang\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">calls hoax</a>, odds of <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4642956-the-ai-safety-bill-rally-is-already-unraveling\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">AI safety law plunge</a>. (0:14) Dave &amp; Buster's <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4642641-dave-busters-swings-to-a-loss-on-negative-comp-sales-higher-operating-costs\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">posts surprise loss</a>. (1:13) Apple's “Widow's Bay” <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4643005-apples-widows-bay-sweeps-emmys-with-14-wins\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">makes Emmy history</a>. (1:57) </p> <p>This is an abridged transcript of the podcast:</p> <p>Our top story so far, while AI companies may join together to pace the frontier, <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4642956-the-ai-safety-bill-rally-is-already-unraveling\">traders don’t think there is much chance of government regulation after President Trump pooh-poohed the idea of a robot revolution.</a></p> <p>With the new cover of Time Magazine saying AI is at an inflection point, odds that the U.S. will pass AI safety legislation this year have tumbled to 17% from a recent peak of 45% on Thursday, when the AI-kills-humanity headlines were going viral. The peak for that contract was 60% in May.</p> <p>Yesterday, <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4642717-trump-calls-ai-a-hoax-in-surprise-onstage-call-with-nvidias-jensen-huang\">Trump dismissed concerns over AI as a “hoax”</a> during a surprise phone call with Nvidia (<span class=\"ticker-hover-wrapper\"><a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/NVDA\" title=\"NVIDIA Corporation\">NVDA</a></span>) CEO Jensen Huang at the All-In Summit in Los Angeles.</p> <p>Huang put the president on speakerphone before the live audience and Trump said, “The robots will not be taking over. The AI will not be taking over the rest of the world.”</p> <p>Huang agreed with Trump that China should be prevented from taking over AI, but also praised former Anthropic (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/ANTHRO\" title=\"Anthropic\">ANTHRO</a>) researcher Jacob Coxon, who resigned over safety concerns, calling him courageous and saying whistleblowers should be taken seriously.</p> <p>Among active stocks, Dave &amp; Buster’s (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/PLAY\" title=\"Dave &amp; Buster's Entertainment, Inc.\">PLAY</a>) <a href=\"https://%20https//seekingalpha.com/news/4642641-dave-busters-swings-to-a-loss-on-negative-comp-sales-higher-operating-costs\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">is sliding as higher food and beverage, payroll, and pre-opening costs eroded Q2 results</a>, driving the company into the red.</p> <p>Enova International (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/ENVA\" title=\"Enova International, Inc.\">ENVA</a>) <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4642757-enova-shares-fall-as-company-withdraws-grasshopper-acquisition-applications\">is plunging after the company withdrew regulatory applications tied to its proposed acquisition of Grasshopper Bancorp.</a></p> <p>CEO Steve Cunningham says regulators “do not have clear standards for nonbanks that want to become banks and that serve customers whose credit needs today are met mostly outside of the banking system.”</p> <p>And ResMed (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/RMD\" title=\"ResMed Inc.\">RMD</a>) <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4642960-resmed-stock-upgraded-rbc-capital-markets\">is up after RBC Capital Markets upgraded the stock to Outperform from Sector Perform and raised its price target to $262 from $244</a>, citing positives in the respiratory device maker’s Q4 results.</p> <p>Analyst Craig Wong-Pan expects high-single-digit EPS growth over the next three years.</p> <p>In other news of note, Apple’s (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/AAPL\" title=\"Apple Inc.\">AAPL</a>) <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4643005-apples-widows-bay-sweeps-emmys-with-14-wins\">series “Widow’s Bay” swept the Emmys comedy category with 14 wins</a>, including best comedy series, best actor, best supporting actress, and best writing and directing, along with awards from last week’s Creative Arts Emmys.</p> <p>The horror/comedy, which follows the exploits of Mayor Tom Loftis trying to boost tourism in his haunted New England town, set a record for the most Emmys won by a comedy series in a single season, beating “The Studio’s” 13 wins last year.</p> <p>Warner Bros. Discovery’s (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/WBD\" title=\"Warner Bros. Discovery, Inc.\">WBD</a>) HBO also came home with trophies for “The Pitt” (best drama and best actor), “DTF St. Louis” (best limited or anthology series), “Task” (best supporting actor), and “Hacks.”</p> <p>And in the Wall Street Research Corner, as predictions abound about what will happen with AI, <a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4642794-a-history-of-good-and-bad-tech-predictions\">Deutsche Bank looked back at some of the best and worst tech predictions of the last century.</a></p> <p>On the prescient side, Nikola Tesla predicted in 1926 that wireless technology would fit into a vest pocket, while computer scientist Ray Kurzweil said in 1999 that computers would have human-level intelligence by 2029.</p> <p>Among the not-so-hot forecasts, Albert Einstein said in 1934 that there was no indication nuclear energy would ever be obtainable. And in 2007, Microsoft (<a href=\"https://seekingalpha.com/symbol/MSFT\" title=\"Microsoft Corporation\">MSFT</a>) CEO Steve Ballmer said the iPhone had no chance of gaining significant market share.</p><p>Editor's Note: This article discusses one or more securities that do not trade on a major U.S. exchange. Please be aware of the risks associated with these stocks.</p></body></html>",
